    <briefdescription>
<para>Deprecated generic strongly-typed wrapper for explicit type conversion. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="since"><para>3.2.0</para>
</simplesect>
The <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1to__t" kindref="compound">to_t</ref></computeroutput> template provides a public, strongly-typed wrapper for any type <computeroutput>T</computeroutput>, enabling explicit conversion of dynamic values and expressions to a type recognised by the µTest++ comparators and reporting mechanisms.</para>
<para>This wrapper inherits from <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1value" kindref="compound">detail::value</ref>&lt;T&gt;</computeroutput>, ensuring that the encapsulated value is treated as the specified type within the framework, for the types without a <computeroutput>to_*</computeroutput> alias, including the application types; with the operators of the <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1operators" kindref="compound">operators</ref></computeroutput> namespace, the comparisons are then reported with their operands.</para>
<para><bold>Example</bold></para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">MyType<sp/>obj;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Explicitly<sp/>treat<sp/>obj<sp/>as<sp/>MyType<sp/>for<sp/>test<sp/>comparison.</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>wrapped<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1to__t_1aad9720f2d1e443d77cdfd1eb1151e924" kindref="member">to_t&lt;MyType&gt;</ref>{obj};</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Deprecated</title><para>Pass the plain value to the function comparators <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1gada610d1d5701b79f3df916f6e397ea06" kindref="member">eq()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1gaa77076edd474fc10d8c0bd6da623e284" kindref="member">ne()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1gaf32fd09749f18635233613fa48f91b56" kindref="member">gt()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1ga989e5966794d5c5487477aa782d844b1" kindref="member">ge()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1gaea39573e23de35872ace5b08d2514327" kindref="member">lt()</ref></computeroutput>, and <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1gaf9e47a6e18771f969cdd840ec187734a" kindref="member">le()</ref></computeroutput> instead; the application types are reported with the <computeroutput>operator&lt;&lt;</computeroutput> of <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1gabecc05360d0941067222d827ff8e3f08" kindref="member">expression_formatter</ref></computeroutput> (since 6.0.0). </para>
</simplesect>
<xrefsect id="deprecated_1_deprecated000031"><xreftitle>Deprecated</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para>pass plain values to <ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1gada610d1d5701b79f3df916f6e397ea06" kindref="member">eq()</ref> and the other comparators (since 6.0.0)</para>
</xrefdescription></xrefsect></para>
    </detaileddescription>
